    <statement><p>A Cartesian equation for the polar equation <m>r=6</m> can be written as:</p>
<p><m>x^2+y^2 =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>36</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>To convert to a Cartesian equation, we use the conversion equation <m>x^2+y^2=r^2</m>.</p>
<p>Squaring both sides of the given polar equation, <m>r=6</m>, gives us 
<me>r = 6\implies r^2 = 36 \implies x^2+y^2 = 36</me></p>
</solution>
